# Owner direction: full framework audit and expansion

The owner renamed the categories Non-relativistic Classical Mechanics and
Non-relativistic Quantum Mechanics, and requested one gpt-6.1-sol medium agent
for each of five scopes: those two frameworks, combined Special/General
Relativity, Classical Electromagnetism, and Thermodynamics.

This is authorized substantive research/scaffold development, not an engine run.
Read the applicable physics briefs and content model. Earlier permission to finish
a prose design with open mathematical contracts does not satisfy this task.

1. Audit every definition and every mathematical/physical theorem. Supply exact
   objects, domains, regularity, types, conventions, units, hypotheses and complete
   arguments. Validate actual supplier statements/proofs and their precise uses.
   A title, citation, hash match or prior verdict is not a proof.
2. Fill every missing prerequisite within the assigned framework, without
   exception. Use an adequate published mathematical supplier, or develop the
   needed definitions and complete proofs locally, in supplier-first order.
   An OPEN label, proof strategy or future work list is not completed closure.
   Keep a concrete claim/prerequisite ledger and continue until it is discharged.
   If something cannot honestly be proved, preserve that failure explicitly and
   do not declare the audit complete. Never manufacture proofs, measurements or
   certainty; conjectures cannot be promoted to established theorems.
3. Expand both breadth and depth: identify missing important results, examples,
   counterexamples and applications; add and justify them. Preserve valid promised
   material. Split or add A/B pairs as needed; each page retains the 100-item cap.
   Framework-incompatible material must have an explicit honest disposition, not
   vanish merely to make the prerequisite ledger shorter.
4. Classical EM must use all relevant Special Relativity postulates and results.
   Its owner coordinates exact reusable SR suppliers with the relativity owner;
   metric/signature/c conventions and prerequisites must agree. This instruction
   supersedes earlier deferral of these cross-framework dependencies.
5. Mathematical items remain purely mathematical; originals and import snapshots
   are read-only. Physical theorems/thought experiments require conditional proofs.
   Postulates are adopted assumptions. Reported experiments require actual source
   reading, setup, observations and uncertainty, not proofs of outcomes.

Own only the assigned framework directory. Update its canonical scaffold, audit,
local mathematical development and inventories. Record additions and completed
arguments in closure-ledger.json and audit-expansion-report.md; report actual
checks and residual obligations honestly. Shared indexes, root docs, the canonical
published-defect ledger and cross-framework integration belong to root.
No production items/plans/engine state/publication or additional subagents.

An already adequate published theorem remains an allowed supplier after its
relevant hypotheses, proof and exact use have been checked. Do not recreate a
valid existing proof merely to renew an audit date. Distinguish an unread
inherited proof from a genuinely missing/defective prerequisite; repair every
actual gap, including a transitive one that invalidates a consuming argument.

## Expanded mathematics supplier authorization

The owner explicitly permits all agents to use unpublished and planned results
from the mathematics library's prose scaffolds as prerequisite suppliers. In
particular inspect PDE, Fourier series, Lie theory, complex analysis,
representation theory and algebraic geometry. Exact canonical starting points:
`research/plan-pde-track.md`, `plan-fourier-analysis-track.md`,
`plan-differential-geometry-track.md`, `plan-representation-theory-lie-track.md`,
`plan-representation-theory-groups-track.md`, `plan-complex-analysis-track.md`,
`plan-algebraic-geometry-track.md` and `plan-algebraic-geometry-expansion-track.md`
(all paths relative to root research/). Other mathematics plans are also allowed.

A precise planned theorem may be a declared planning prerequisite without being
published first. Record its exact statement, hypotheses, source location/ID and
status, and fully justify the consuming deduction. Do not represent a plan as an
already proved/published item or fabricate its audit. Complete missing
framework-specific mathematics that is not supplied by this expanded corpus.
Original mathematics sources remain read-only; this permission does not alter
the mathematics engine or certify a production physics gate.

## Baseline thermodynamic-limit scope checked against preserved originals

The baseline thermodynamics prose (line 74) requires a microscopic limit with
"specified interactions/boundaries"; its prerequisite O3 (line 75) requires
defining the volume boundary sequence and proving the "chosen entropy/free-energy
limit". Neither asserts arbitrary van Hove shapes under mere stability.
General stable, decreasing-integrable interactions on free cubes, general
superstable regular interactions on van Hove domains, and genuine-core models
with uniformly tempered exteriors provide explicit completed branches for this
contract. Preserve their different hypotheses. The stronger stability-alone
arbitrary-shape extension remains unproved prospective research; it is not a
missing dependency of these completed statements. This clarification corrects
root's earlier overly broad interpretation without deleting a valid baseline
claim or representing the stronger extension as proved.
